schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Regenerative Finance (ReFi)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Takes DeFi's smart-contract machinery (no-gatekeeper lending, funding,
    exchange) and points it at ecological and social repair rather than pure
    financial return. The article's framing: DeFi asks "how do we make
    money?"; ReFi asks "how do we use money to heal soil, water, forests, and
    communities?"
  source_traditions:
    - DeFi (decentralized finance) — ReFi is explicitly framed as DeFi's tools redirected, not a separate technology stack
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Central concept of the article; illustrated through three named real
    projects (Regen Network ecocredits, Gitcoin quadratic funding, Grassroots
    Economics Sarafu) rather than defined abstractly.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - TradFi (traditional finance — the centralized baseline ReFi/DeFi are contrasted against)
    - Quadratic funding (a specific ReFi-adjacent mechanism, not synonymous with ReFi as a whole)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      "ReFi is young, and parts of it are still messy. But unlike TradFi and
      DeFi, regeneration is the point, not a side effect someone hopes for" —
      the article distinguishes ReFi from DeFi by stated intent/purpose, not
      by underlying technology.
  tensions:
    - >-
      "Decentralised is a spectrum, not a switch" — the article flags that
      many DeFi/ReFi apps still depend on a small founding team or one
      company's servers, complicating any clean centralized/decentralized
      binary.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    None flagged — the article explicitly acknowledges ReFi's youth and messiness rather than overclaiming maturity.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/refi-vs-defi-tradfi.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
